WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:08.160
Kashmir…a paradise that draws visitors from
all over the world.

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:14.110
But, ever since a major terror attack and
strikes by India and Pakistan, they've stayed

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:19.600
away - crippling the region’s key tourism
industry.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:25.240
Mohammad Shafi has been ferrying people across
Srinagar's famous Dal Lake in his shikhara,

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:29.300
a typical Kashmiri boat, since he was a young
boy.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:34.649
The recent turmoil has scared away his clients
and decimated his earnings.

00:00:34.649 --> 00:00:40.059
"There are about 4,000 boat owners here.

00:00:40.059 --> 00:00:41.760
They’ve all lost their business.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:45.899
It’s a terrible situation."

00:00:45.899 --> 00:00:51.539
Shafi and his friends have seen their income
wax and wane over the years - in line with

00:00:51.539 --> 00:00:56.959
the militant attacks, protests and crackdowns
that periodically inflame tensions in the

00:00:56.959 --> 00:00:59.030
Indian-held parts of the region.

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:05.119
"I don’t know what the problems between
India and Pakistan are…Kashmir is passed

00:01:05.119 --> 00:01:06.960
like a football between the two.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:13.850
It’s just used politically."

00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:19.500
It's a sentiment shared by many on the streets
of Srinagar in Indian-administered Kashmir.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.280
Soldiers are everywhere.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:26.490
The recent war games between India and Pakistan
have added to the sense of unease.

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:29.310
No one was willing to speak out on camera.

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:35.150
"While tensions between India and Pakistan
are winding down after last week’s aerial

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:39.910
strikes, a climate of fear prevails in the
heavily militarized Kashmir Valley.

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:46.310
Here, in downtown Srinagar, shops and businesses
have opened today after days of intermittent

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:54.700
strikes and shutdowns, causing major disruptions
to daily life."

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:59.400
Riyaz Wani's first thought was to stock up
on rice and fuel when tensions erupted over

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.750
Kashmir last week.

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:09.729
He’s been through decades of shutdowns and
curfews - and even started his own kitchen

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:13.599
garden in his backyard to prepare for an emergency.

00:02:13.599 --> 00:02:19.480
But, the father of two was terrified for his
family when India and Pakistan engaged in

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:24.459
retaliatory aerial strikes last week - just
a few hundred kilometers from here - putting

00:02:24.459 --> 00:02:27.450
the entire region on edge.

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:31.030
"Those days were very scary for us.

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:32.939
Jets thundered overhead.

00:02:32.939 --> 00:02:36.150
We heard the news that one or two jets were
brought down.

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:39.969
People who got killed .. maybe the two countries
will talk now.

00:02:39.969 --> 00:02:42.909
That will be better for every one."

00:02:42.909 --> 00:02:47.799
The conflict in Kashmir has dragged on for
decades.

00:02:47.799 --> 00:02:53.769
For people here, peace remains elusive in
this beautiful but cursed Himalayan valley

00:02:53.769 --> 00:02:54.949
that both nations claim.

